### =====================================================================
### Phase 5: expenses, payments, cash and personal accounts
### Uses October 2026 (opened in the Phase 4 file). Send top to bottom.
### Member ids: manager = 1, Srijila = 2 (check with GET /api/months/2026/10).
### Update the manager password in step 1 if you changed it.
### =====================================================================

@base = http://localhost:8080/api
@month = {{base}}/months/2026/10
@managerId = 1
@srijilaId = 2


### 1. Log in as the manager
# @name managerLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "manager", "password": "changeme123" }

@managerToken = {{managerLogin.response.body.token}}


### ---------------- Starting figures copied from your spreadsheet ----------------

### 2. Opening CASH: the manager already holds 1000 of flat cash
POST {{month}}/cash/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holderMemberId": {{managerId}}, "amount": 1000, "type": "OPENING", "reason": "Cash in hand when we started the app" }


### 3. Opening DUE: the manager owed 300 from last month's spreadsheet
POST {{month}}/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": {{managerId}}, "amount": 300, "type": "OPENING", "reason": "Due from September spreadsheet" }


### 4. Opening CREDIT: Srijila had 200 credit (negative = credit)
POST {{month}}/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": {{srijilaId}}, "amount": -200, "type": "OPENING", "reason": "Credit from September spreadsheet" }


### ---------------- Expenses ----------------

### 5. Groceries paid from flat cash held by the manager → 201
POST {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-10-05", "category": "Groceries", "description": "Weekly market",
  "amount": 9000, "fundedBy": "FLAT_CASH", "holderMemberId": {{managerId}} }


### 6. Same expense again → 409 "already exists ... allowDuplicate"
POST {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-10-05", "category": "Groceries", "amount": 9000,
  "fundedBy": "FLAT_CASH", "holderMemberId": {{managerId}} }


### 7. Srijila buys fish with her OWN money → her account gets 2000 credit
POST {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-10-08", "category": "Fish", "amount": 2000,
  "fundedBy": "MEMBER_POCKET", "holderMemberId": {{srijilaId}} }


### 8. A mistaken expense (we'll void it next)
# @name mistake
POST {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-10-09", "category": "Oops", "amount": 123.45,
  "fundedBy": "FLAT_CASH", "holderMemberId": {{managerId}} }


### 9. Void it with a reason (kept in history, no longer counted)
POST {{month}}/expenses/{{mistake.response.body.id}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Entered by mistake" }


### 10. All expenses (the voided one shows "status": "VOIDED")
GET {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### ---------------- Payments and cash ----------------

### 11. Srijila pays 4500, the manager receives the cash
POST {{month}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": {{srijilaId}}, "cashHolderId": {{managerId}}, "amount": 4500, "paidOn": "2026-10-10" }


### 12. The manager pays her own share, 5000, and keeps the cash
POST {{month}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "memberId": {{managerId}}, "cashHolderId": {{managerId}}, "amount": 5000, "paidOn": "2026-10-10" }


### 13. The manager hands 300 of flat cash to Srijila for vegetables (a transfer, not income or expense)
POST {{month}}/cash/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromMemberId": {{managerId}}, "toMemberId": {{srijilaId}}, "amount": 300, "transferredOn": "2026-10-12" }


### 14. Srijila spends 250 of that flat cash on vegetables
POST {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expenseDate": "2026-10-12", "category": "Vegetables", "amount": 250,
  "fundedBy": "FLAT_CASH", "holderMemberId": {{srijilaId}} }


### 15. The manager counts her cash: 1150 in hand.
###     Recorded should be 1000 + 4500 + 5000 - 9000 - 300 = 1200, so step 18 shows SHORT by 50.
POST {{month}}/cash/counts
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holderMemberId": {{managerId}}, "countedAmount": 1150, "note": "Counted at month end" }


### ---------------- Reports ----------------

### 16. Live meal rate (now uses the real expenses)
GET {{month}}/meal-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### 17. Everyone's personal accounts (manager only)
GET {{month}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### 18. Cash per holder + reconciliation (recorded vs counted)
GET {{month}}/cash
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### ---------------- As Srijila ----------------

### 19. Log in as Srijila
# @name memberLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "srijila", "password": "srijila-pass-123" }

@memberToken = {{memberLogin.response.body.token}}


### 20. Her own account → 200 (her credit includes the 2000 fish; the 50 cash she holds is NOT credit)
GET {{month}}/accounts/me
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 21. Everyone's accounts → 403
GET {{month}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 22. The manager's account → 403
GET {{month}}/accounts/{{managerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 23. Payments list → 403
GET {{month}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}


### 24. Shared expenses → 200 (everyone can see what the flat spent)
GET {{month}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
